{"id":29464,"slug":"the-daytrippers","title":"The Daytrippers","year":1996,"country":"Canada, United States","duration":87,"spine":1001,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/29464-the-daytrippers","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/films/970a3900ccacf0352f032e35c13549ed/un35TUcekpTvbbRD0VsNDeM3k57TjF_large.jpg","description":"\nWith its droll humor and bittersweet emotional heft, the feature debut of writer-director Greg Mottola announced the arrival of an unassumingly sharp-witted new talent on the 1990s indie film scene. When she discovers a love letter written to her husband (Stanley Tucci) by an unknown paramour, the distraught Eliza (Hope Davis) turns to her tight-knit Long Island family for advice. Soon the entire clan—strong-willed mom (Anne Meara), taciturn dad (Pat McNamara), and jaded sister (Parker Posey) with pretentious boyfriend (Liev Schreiber) in tow—has squeezed into a station wagon and headed into Manhattan to find out the truth, kicking off a one-crazy-day odyssey full of unexpected detours and life-changing revelations. Performed with deadpan virtuosity by a top-flight ensemble cast, The Daytrippers is a wry and piercing look at family bonds stretched to the breaking point.","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"Greg Mottola","slug":"greg-mottola"}],"cast":[{"actor":"Hope Davis","role":"Eliza","slug":"hope-davis"},{"actor":"Pat McNamara","role":"Jim Malone","slug":"pat-mcnamara"},{"actor":"Anne Meara","role":"Rita Malone","slug":"anne-meara"},{"actor":"Parker Posey","role":"Jo","slug":"parker-posey"},{"actor":"Liev Schreiber","role":"Carl","slug":"liev-schreiber"},{"actor":"Campbell Scott","role":"Eddie","slug":"campbell-scott"},{"actor":"Stanley Tucci","role":"Louis","slug":"stanley-tucci"},{"actor":"Andy Brown","role":"Ronnie","slug":"andy-brown"},{"actor":"Marc Grapey","role":"Aaron","slug":"marc-grapey"},{"actor":"Marcia Gay Harden","role":"Libby","slug":"marcia-gay-harden"},{"actor":"Marcia Haufrecht","role":"Moll